Z||000000||Jncomutt||04-09-2001||09:06 PM||||I have an 84 Fiero I wanna upgrade the sound system in.  I was lookin for some info on the headrest speakers.  What size are they? What it takes to change them, and any recommendations if anyone here has done this...  I've heard a lot about adding subwoofers behind the seats, or swappin out the 4x10's in the dash for two 4" but can't seem to find anything on the headrest.<P>When I went down to the local Circuit City, the guy wanted nothin to do with them.  In fact he told me to just buy some "good 4x10's" (didn't know those existed) and leave the headrest disconnected!  Some customer service, I'd say....<P>Any information would be greatly appreciated.<p>[This message has been edited by Jncomutt (edited 04-09-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000001||Oreif||04-09-2001||09:20 PM||||Headrest speakers are 3 1/2" speakers. Many brands are available. To replace them you need to remove the seat back covers. (a zipper and hogrings) I have replaced a few for friends. We usually use the Polk Audio's or the Pioneer's but there are many brands available. I have heard of putting 4" speakers in the seats but I have not seen it done. (I personally think it's overkill with as close to your head as the speakers sit) Remember you need to buy 2 pairs. 1 Pair for each seat.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||04-09-2001||11:49 PM||||If you're going to get some 4x10s for the dash, check these out. I don't have them, but I've heard from other forum members that they sound good.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006738.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/006738.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily overheating)||||reg||14
Z||000003||drednot||04-09-2001||11:51 PM||||I like the stock headrest speekers.  They sound good to me and they have no foam to disolve.||||reg||1
